"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[7304],{47304:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"klyuchevaya-stavka-23-oktyabrya-2026-pauza","locale":"en","title":"25 of 26 economists expect the Bank of Russia to hold its rate at 14% on October 23","description":"Almost all economists expect the Bank of Russia to retain a 14% rate on October 23, 2026. Why a pause is expected and what it means for deposits and loans.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"On October 23, 2026, the Bank of Russia\'s board will announce its key-rate decision and update its macroeconomic forecast. Of 26 economists surveyed, 25 expect the rate to remain at 14%; one expects a cut to 13.75%. Sberbank first deputy chairman Alexander Vedyakhin also calls a hold the most likely outcome. From June 6, 2025, the rate was reduced from 21% to 14% in July 2026, before the first pause on September 11. Some economists think the pause may last until year-end. The final 2026 meeting is scheduled for December 18."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Prices explain the pause. They rose by 6.1% from January 1 to October 12; annual inflation is 7.22% by the Economy Ministry\'s estimate, against the regulator\'s 2026 forecast of 6–7%. Bank of Russia Governor Elvira Nabiullina explained on September 11 that one-off factors beyond the rate\'s influence had halted easing. The regulator included production disruptions and expensive fuel among them. However, it also estimated underlying inflation excluding temporary spikes at an annualized 5–6%, above its 4% target."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Expectations show how a temporary jump can become persistent. Imagine a hairdresser expecting rent and hair dye to rise by 14% over a year. They raise haircut prices now. A customer also expecting higher prices buys a television today before it becomes dearer, using credit. Prices rise because people expect them to rise. These are inflation expectations. In September, households expected 14.2% inflation over the following year, up from 13.7% in August and almost twice the actual 7.22%."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"The Bank of Russia has named another condition: rate cuts in 2027 depend on whether the budget deficit narrows. When the state spends more than it receives, additional demand enters the economy and prices rise faster."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"For depositors, a pause means deposit rates hold up. The average maximum rate at the 10 largest banks was 13.05% in late September. For borrowers, loans and unsubsidized mortgages remain expensive. If the rate stays unchanged on October 23, the next opportunity for a cut will not come until December 18."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"A depositor opening a one-year account now locks in about 13%. They benefit if rate cuts begin sooner than economists expect, but miss higher interest if rates must rise. A borrower waiting for cheap credit faces at least another 2 months while prices continue rising. The October 23 macroeconomic forecast will show how long the Bank of Russia intends to keep rates high."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"What key-rate decision is expected on October 23, 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"Almost all economists expect a hold at 14%. In a survey of 26 economists, 25 gave that answer; one expects a cut to 13.75%. Sberbank also considers a hold the most likely outcome."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Why is the Bank of Russia not cutting rates?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"Prices have risen by 6.1% since the start of the year, close to the upper end of the Bank of Russia\'s 6–7% forecast. Part of the jump is temporary, caused by expensive fuel and production disruptions. But households expect 14.2% inflation over the next year, and the regulator fears temporary acceleration may become persistent."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"What does the pause in rate cuts mean for deposits and mortgages?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"With the rate at 14%, deposits remain attractive: the average maximum rate at major banks was 13.05% in late September. Loans and unsubsidized mortgages remain expensive. After October 23, the Bank of Russia\'s next decision is scheduled for December 18."}],"sources":[{"label":"Vedomosti consensus forecast: economists almost unanimously expect a central-bank pause","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/economics/articles/2026/10/16/1237503-konsensus-prognoz-vedomostei"},{"label":"Sberbank expects the key rate to remain unchanged","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9026103"},{"label":"Sber expects the central bank to hold rates after its October meeting","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1122297"},{"label":"Inflation expectations and consumer sentiment, September 2026","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/analytics/dkp/inflationary_expectations/Infl_exp_26-09/"},{"label":"Russian inflation for October 6–12 is 0.11%","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1122459"},{"label":"Bank of Russia publishes its 2026 key-rate meeting schedule","url":"https://finance.mail.ru/article/bank-rossii-opublikoval-grafik-zasedaniy-po-klyuchevoy-stavke-na-2026-god-68067122/"},{"label":"Average maximum deposit rate at ten banks rises to 13.05%","url":"https://ria.ru/20261001/bank-2121443529.html"},{"label":"Bank of Russia cuts the key rate to 20% annually","url":"https://finance.mail.ru/article/bank-rossii-snizil-klyuchevuyu-stavku-do-20-godovyh-66466367/"},{"label":"Bank of Russia raises its 2026 inflation forecast","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/8843971"}],"sourceBodySha256":"fe62eaf826a4de568479af2c8bab712a15f8ab8a8d9f9a89aca0a2ed2e59bfc4"}')}}]);